<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 89,115 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 89,115 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 89,115 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 55,684 tonnes on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	 Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			26,968	     7,500</p>
<p>    Import cargo			62,147	    48,184</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, two ships sailed and seven berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven ships are expected to sail and 11 to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity	     Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		 Berthing</p>
<p>Fuel oil		36,000	 Yasmeen	    due</p>
<p>General cargo	  8,630	 Feng Mao	   due</p>
<p>General cargo	  1,164	 Karlina	    26/6</p>
<p>High speed diesel   28,313	 Apsheron	   27/6</p>
<p>Gas oil		 60,000	 CSP-10	     1/7</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
